INFO 7804 :: Page 146 :: 840 P. M Winchester Va Mar 5th 1865 for Genl Torbert. Willards Hotel Gen Hancocks HdQrs go to Cumberland tomorrow or next day ---- Morgan says but temporarily will you be here Monday night (sig) Wm Russell Asst Adjt Genl 920 P. M 9.25 P. M Fort Monroe Mar 5th 65 Newberne, March 1st Via Ft Monroe 8.30 PM 5th to W. . Whiton two fifty G St Washn. Order every cars belonging to U. S Mil RR now on foreign Roads returned to Alexandria immediately. Direct that the Potomac R. R. be operated separately from Balto and Ohio reshipping freight at H Ferry Send at the earliest possible moment narrow gauge stock as follows. Two 2 Engines fifteen flat and fifteen box cars to Wilmington N. C and of the same gauge two Engines twenty five flat and twenty five box cars to Morehead City N. C. or if possible to secure vessels of proper draught to Newberne to which place there is eight and one half feet of water over the bar. Do not fail to have these shipments made at once. the case is desperate. Make requisition upon QmGenl for fifty box cars narrow gauge and have Cal Robinson see that they are manufactured as early as possible. On receipt of this telegraph me at 5th Avenue Hotel L. C. McCallum Br Gen Supt MRR
INFO 7832 :: Page 174 :: 1040 PM 22 Ft Monroe Mar 21 1865 830 pm dated HdQrs armies U. S. 22d Gen JA Ekin 1st Divn QrMrGen office ---- It is supposed Sheridan will be here by the twenty seventh prepared for another march with the exception of two thousand cavalry horses ---- the Lt Genl directs me to obtain all that you can possibly send me on time ---- Both these armies require a large number yet ---- please forward as rapidly as possible ---- If Sheridan does not detain our transports unnecessarily at White House Genl Rucker should be able to furnish sufficient transportation ---- Rufus Ingalls Br Gen Chf Q. M. &c 1230 AM 23d City Point Va Mch 22d 7 PM 22d Maj Gen Augur --- you may send the 5th Mass cavalry as it is transportation & all U Grant Lt Genl 1 AM 23d City Point Mch 22d 1865 8 PM 21d For Br Gen Hoffman you may reduce the number of prisoners forwarded here for delivery to two thousand per week until further notice ---- US Grant Lt Gen
INFO 7835 :: Page 177 :: 530 P. M. New York Mar. 23.1865 Hon C. A. Dana Asst Sec War, ---- Send privately for T. P. Marsh clerk under Col S. L Brown Chf of 5th Divn 2 m Dept ---- Tell him all of Brown's rascalities are discovered & his only safety is in telling all he knows ---- then on some pretext send him to me for examination Signed H. S. Olcott Col & Spl. Comd 6 PM St. Louis Mar. 23. 1865. for Gen Halleck I shall start for Arkansas day after tomorrow unless the Gen in Chf wishes me to wait here for instruction I shall probably be about twelve or 14 days please inform me if he wishes me to await instructions here ---- Jno Pope Maj Gen Cmdg. 230 pm 240 pm 24 City Point Mch 23d 1865 Gen Halleck ---- Have you heard anything from Crufts command which left Nashville on the 14th for Newberne? US Grant Lt Genl
INFO 8651 :: Page 173 :: 630 pm City Point Mch 21st 1865 230 pm 20th for Secy of War I would recommend relieving Crook from command of his Dept and ordering him to command the Cavalry of the Army of the Potomac . I would call attention to the fact that our white troops are being paid whilst the colored troops are not if paymasters <insertion>could be</insertion> ordered here immediately to commence paying them it would have a fine effect . US Grant Lt Genl McCaine Winchester Washn Mch 21st 1865 730 pm for Maj E O Parsons Provost Marshal . Do you want any more evidence in the case of Charles E Langley if so let me know immediately I have an important witness (sig) Wm H Weigel Major and acting Pro Mar
INFO 8654 :: Page 176 :: Mch 11th 1865 2 PM 24th South West Pass Via N Orleans N Orleans Mch 10th ---- Gen Grant ---- Va ---- Gen Canby left here Mch 5th for Mobile Bay where Grangers command & AJ Smith commands now are with the exception of two or three thousand men who are now getting off ---- Steele with about eight thousand men is at Pens - a - - coala probably to move on Blakely ---- Grierson is here & his cavalry coming He goes I am told to Canby & it will take him a week to get his command there ---- much delay has been caused by a cipher clerks blunder which made AJ Smith land at Vicksburg & discharge his steam boats ---- Rebels supposed to have nine thousand men at Mobile & as many at Blakely sig ---- very cold here today CB Comstock
